    "body": "fix on issue/2343-rotary-parallel-held-end · PR #2675 · pinned by continuous_4axis_part::the_pass_leaves_the_chuck_side_end_face, continuous_4axis_part::a_short_flute_posts_now_that_the_chuck_side_end_face_is_left, rotary::the_parallel_leaves_the_end_face_where_the_stock_goes_on, multiaxis::rotary_ends::tests · merges when reviewed\n\nRotary Parallel now reads the stock. Where the stock goes on past an end of the model by more than one tool diameter, the centre of the ball does not go past that end plane, and a note names the end. This PR adds no setting for an axial window: that is a `feat`, and `docs/decisions/2343-rotary-parallel-held-end.md` has the reasons.\n",
